// Title: Sysmon Driver Unloaded Via Fltmc.EXE
// Sigma ID: 4d7cda18-1b12-4e52-b45c-d28653210df8
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Kirill Kiryanov, oscd.community
// Date: 2019-10-23 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: stealth, defense-impairment, T1070, T1685, T1685.001
// Description: Detects possible Sysmon filter driver unloaded via fltmc.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.darkoperator.com/blog/2018/10/5/operating-offensively-against-sysmon
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_fltmc_unload_driver_sysmon.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\fltMC.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "fltMC.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "unload" and ProcessCommandLine contains "sysmon")
